diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c4ad123..47cc0d2 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,3 +1,14 @@
+> **This is a modified version of Realistic Water, not the original mod.**
+> Original mod by **Skaffy**: https://github.com/sskaffy/Realistic-Water
+> Distributed under the original license (see `LICENSE`), with that notice kept intact.
+>
+> **What this fork changes (hardware compatibility):**
+> - Reads the GPU's real limits from Vulkan at startup and logs them.
+> - The pressure solver no longer requires 1024-thread workgroups: it uses the largest size the GPU supports (down to the Vulkan minimum of 128), and sizes the coarsest grid level to match.
+> - GPUs without subgroup arithmetic/ballot in compute shaders get a working fallback instead of failing to compile.
+> - Compiled shaders are cached on disk (`.minecraft/.cache/realistic-water/spirv`), and one shader compiler is reused, so later launches start faster.
+> - New `hardwareProfile` setting (`/water`, Performance): on `auto`, integrated GPUs and GPUs with under 3 GB of VRAM get lighter defaults (lower resolution, fewer substeps, simpler surface). Settings you changed yourself are never overridden; `full` turns this off.
+
 # Realistic Water
 A Minecraft mod that adds a lot of cool, realistic stuff from Minecraft Blender animations.
 
